<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cairo Citadel</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Citadel of Cairo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a> Citadel is a medieval Islamic fortress on the Muqattam hills in Cairo. It was begun by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> in the 1170s as part of the Ayyubid fortification of the city. It served as the seat of government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> for several centuries under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a> and its successors.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cairo-citadel.jpg" alt="Cairo Citadel" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ahmed Al.Badawy from Cairo, Egypt · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flickr_-_HuTect_ShOts_-_Citadel_of_Salah_El.Din_and_Masjid_Muhammad_Ali_%D9%82%D9%84%D8%B9%D8%A9_%D8%B5%D9%84%D8%A7%D8%AD_%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AF%D9%8A%D9%86_%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%A3%D9%8A%D9%88%D8%A8%D9%8A_%D9%88%D9%85%D8%B3%D8%AC%D8%AF_%D9%85%D8%AD%D9%85%D8%AF_%D8%B9%D9%84%D9%8A_-_Cairo_-_Egypt_-_17_04_2010_(4).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
